  "body_html": "<h1>Sequential Equilibrium</h1>\n<p>A pair $(\\beta,\\mu)$ is a sequential equilibrium if it is weak Bayesian perfect and\nthere exists a sequence of completely mixed behavioral profiles $\\beta^n$ converging\nto $\\beta$ such that the Bayes-rule beliefs $\\nu_{\\beta^n}$ converge to $\\mu$.</p>\n<p>Thus off-path beliefs must arise as limits of beliefs generated by fully mixed\ntrembling strategies.</p>",
